          %h3#charts_for_mapping_spaces Charts for Mapping Spaces
          %p Local additions are used to great effect in constructing charts for mapping spaces.
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a smooth manifold (possibly infinite dimensional). Let
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            be a functionally compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%B6licher+space"} Frölicher space
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \subseteq M
            be a submanifold. Let
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \subseteq N
            be a subset. We consider the space
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_72.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo ;
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(N,M;Q,P)
            of smooth maps
            %math#mathml_26ecd24cbcd4290244c987e7239084dea2eb07d3_73.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
